
## Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- Docker & Docker Compose
- Python 3.11+

### Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/tahaelqassid/fx-pnl-trading-room.git
cd fx-pnl-trading-room
cp .env.example .env   # fill in your credentials and API keys
docker compose up -d
pip install -r requirements.txt

python ingestion/load_csv.py
cd fx_pnl_dbt && dbt deps && dbt run && dbt test && cd ..
python engine/run_daily_pnl.py
```

### Launch the dashboard

```bash
streamlit run dashboard/app.py
```

### Run tests

```bash
python tests/test_case_study.py
python tests/test_risk_model.py
```

## Validation

The calculation engine is validated against a reference case study. During development, this process surfaced two real defects: an arithmetic inconsistency in the source specification's worked FIFO example, and a cross-currency valuation error in the EUR/USD synthetic cross, both corrected and independently re-verified across the Python engine and the dbt SQL layer.

| Indicator | Value |
|---|---|
| Total daily P&L (MTM) | +79,460 MAD |
| Realized P&L | +20,000 MAD |
| Unrealized P&L | +59,460 MAD |
| FIFO P&L on 600K USD | +22,000 MAD |
| WAC P&L on 600K USD | +18,000 MAD |

## Known Limitations

- Single-currency case study data; schema is multi-currency-ready but not yet exercised with a second accounting currency
- Market-structure signal is a technical-analysis heuristic, not a validated predictive model — not investment advice
- Real trading-room data is confidential and unavailable; the project uses a documented case study and simulated live feed instead

